      <!-- THE VERDICT FIRST -->
      <div class="verdict-box">
        <div class="verdict-label">Bottom line</div>
        <p class="verdict-text"><strong>Marek Health wins on value.</strong> At $140/mo it scores higher (8.0 vs 7.7), has a cleaner physician model, and costs $660/year less than Defy. But Defy Medical has a legitimate use case: men who want a functional-medicine approach with peptide therapy options. If that's you, Defy is worth the premium. If you want traditional TRT with MD oversight, Marek is the pick — and it's not close.</p>
      </div>

