      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;color:var(--ink);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;padding-bottom:0.6rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--border);">Who should pick which</h2>

      <div class="pros-cons" style="margin:1.25rem 0 2rem;">
        <div class="pros-box" style="background:rgba(13,107,62,0.05);border-color:rgba(13,107,62,0.18);">
          <h3 style="color:#0d6b3e;">Pick Defy Medical if…</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You want peptide therapy alongside your TRT (BPC-157, TB-500, KLOW)</li>
            <li>You prefer a functional/integrative approach to hormone health</li>
            <li>You want a broader health optimization plan, not just testosterone management</li>
            <li>You've used TRT before and want a more comprehensive stack</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cons-box" style="background:rgba(29,78,216,0.05);border-color:rgba(29,78,216,0.18);">
          <h3 style="color:#1d4ed8;">Pick Marek Health if…</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You want strong MD-only oversight on every prescription</li>
            <li>You're primarily focused on TRT without a broader peptide stack</li>
            <li>Value matters — $140/mo vs $195/mo is $660/year you keep</li>
            <li>You want a traditional physician relationship (not a wellness platform)</li>
            <li>You're newer to TRT and want a straightforward, proven approach</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
